.TH OROC-VERSIONS 1 "" "Oro Runtime 0.1.2" "Oro Runtime Manual"
.SH NAME
oroc\-versions \- Print Oro CLI/runtime and dependency versions.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
oroc versions [options] [<dependency\-name>]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Print Oro CLI/runtime and dependency versions.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-f, \-\-format=<format>\fR
print as 'text' or 'json'
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
shorthand for '\-\-format=json'
.TP
\fB\-V, \-\-verbose\fR
enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-file=<path>\fR
mirror logs to a JSON file
.SH NOTES
.PP
With no dependency name, prints the full version map for the CLI, runtime, and linked libraries. Passing a dependency name filters to a single entry (for example: oro, oroc, uv, sqlite, iroh). Use '\-\-json' or '\-\-format=json' when you need stable machine\-readable output on stdout. Use '\-\-log\-file=<path>' if you also need logs; the global 'oroc \-\-json ...' form is reserved for JSON log streaming.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBoroc versions\fR
print all known dependency versions as text
.TP
\fBoroc versions \-\-json\fR
print all known dependency versions as JSON
.TP
\fBoroc versions uv\fR
print only the libuv version
.SH SEE ALSO
oroc(1)
